# Landsat Remote Sensing Pipeline (2010–2026)

Replace the Sentinel-2 pipeline (data only from ~2015) with a **Landsat-based pipeline** that provides continuous 30m-resolution remote sensing data from **2010 to 2026** for all districts in UP, Haryana, and Punjab.

## Why Landsat?

| Satellite | Availability | Resolution | GEE Collection |
|-----------|-------------|------------|----------------|
| Landsat 5 TM | 1984–2013 | 30m | `LANDSAT/LT05/C02/T1_L2` |
| Landsat 7 ETM+ | 1999–present | 30m | `LANDSAT/LE07/C02/T1_L2` |
| Landsat 8 OLI | 2013–present | 30m | `LANDSAT/LC08/C02/T1_L2` |
| Landsat 9 OLI-2 | 2021–present | 30m | `LANDSAT/LC09/C02/T1_L2` |

By combining all 4 sensors, we get **seamless coverage from 2010 to 2026**. All use USGS Collection 2 Level-2 (surface reflectance), already atmospherically corrected.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Band Mapping**: Landsat 5/7 use different band names (e.g., `SR_B4` = NIR) than Landsat 8/9 (e.g., `SR_B5` = NIR). The pipeline will harmonize these automatically.

> [!WARNING]
> **Landsat 7 SLC-off**: After May 2003, Landsat 7 has striping artifacts. We use it only as a gap-filler when Landsat 5/8 data is unavailable, and the compositing approach minimizes the impact.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Band Selection**: The Sentinel-2 pipeline extracted B7, B8, B8A, B12 (NIR/Red Edge/SWIR). For Landsat, the closest equivalents are:
> - **NIR** (Landsat B4/B5) ↔ Sentinel-2 B8
> - **SWIR1** (Landsat B5/B6) ↔ Sentinel-2 B8A (approximate)
> - **SWIR2** (Landsat B7) ↔ Sentinel-2 B12
> - **Red** (Landsat B3/B4) — no direct Red Edge equivalent, but useful for NDVI
>
> The output CSV will have columns: `NIR`, `SWIR1`, `SWIR2`, `Red` instead of `B7`, `B8`, `B8A`, `B12`. Is this acceptable?

## Proposed Changes

All files will be created in a **new folder**: `Remote sensing data/landsat_wheat_pipeline/`

---

### Pipeline Structure

```
landsat_wheat_pipeline/
├── config.py                    # Configuration (bands, districts, years 2010-2025)
├── gee_extractor.py             # Multi-sensor Landsat extractor via GEE
├── fill_missing_sma.py          # SMA gap-filling (same logic as Sentinel-2)
├── process_all_districts.py     # Multi-year orchestrator with resume capability
├── __init__.py                  # Package init
├── requirements.txt             # Dependencies
├── README.md                    # Documentation
└── output/                      # Created at runtime
    ├── raw/                     # Per-district per-year raw CSVs
    ├── filled/                  # SMA-filled CSVs
    ├── merged/                  # Multi-year merged CSVs per district
    └── logs/                    # Processing logs
```

---

### [NEW] [config.py](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Remote%20sensing%20data/landsat_wheat_pipeline/config.py)

- Same district lists (22 Haryana + 23 Punjab + 75 UP)
- `PROCESSING_YEARS = list(range(2010, 2026))` → 16 years
- Landsat band definitions with cross-sensor mapping table
- Same wheat season config (Oct–Apr), same 5-day composites (42 time steps)
- Quality control thresholds adapted for Landsat (cloud cover flags differ)

---

### [NEW] [gee_extractor.py](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Remote%20sensing%20data/landsat_wheat_pipeline/gee_extractor.py)

Key differences from Sentinel-2 version:
- `LandsatExtractor` class instead of [Sentinel2Extractor](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Remote%20sensing%20data/sentinel2_wheat_pipeline/gee_extractor.py#22-537)
- **Multi-sensor merging**: Automatically selects the right Landsat sensor(s) per year:
  - 2010–2012: Landsat 5 + Landsat 7 (fallback)
  - 2013: Landsat 7 + Landsat 8
  - 2014–2020: Landsat 8 + Landsat 7 (fallback)
  - 2021+: Landsat 8 + Landsat 9
- **Band harmonization**: Renames bands to common names (`NIR`, `SWIR1`, `SWIR2`, `Red`)
- **Cloud masking**: Uses `QA_PIXEL` bitmask (Landsat C2 L2 standard) instead of Sentinel-2 QA60
- **Cropland mask**: Same ESA WorldCover 2021 approach
- Same district geometry resolution (GAUL boundaries + point-buffer fallback)
- Same CSV output format (state, district, year, time_step, dates, bands, quality)

---

### [NEW] [fill_missing_sma.py](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Remote%20sensing%20data/landsat_wheat_pipeline/fill_missing_sma.py)

- Nearly identical to Sentinel-2 version
- Updated band column names: `['NIR', 'SWIR1', 'SWIR2', 'Red']`

